// The Interceptor interface, v2: one message at a time
// (docs/INTERCEPTOR_V2.md).
//
// The customer runs a gRPC server implementing Interceptor; AIntercept's
// observer is the client. A deployment picks v1 or v2
// (interceptor.contract); v1 is the default.
//
// v2 hands the Interceptor the conversation, not the wire: OnRequest carries
// only the messages a call adds (not the history every call resends), in one
// shape for Anthropic Messages, OpenAI Responses (HTTP and Codex's
// WebSocket) and Chat Completions. Its answers come back per message, and
// AIntercept puts them back on the wire in the provider's format.
//
//   observe  Callbacks are delivered asynchronously; answers are recorded,
//            never applied.
//   enforce  OnCallStart, OnRequest, OnReply and OnToolCall are in the
//            call's path, within the deadline; answers are applied. On a
//            failure or a missed deadline the call is refused (fail closed;
//            configurable).
//
// Content: OnRequest, OnReply and OnToolCall are only called when the
// deployment enables Interceptor content. Every message goes to the
// Interceptor in both directions: the request's new messages before they go
// upstream, and the reply's text and tool calls before the client sees them.
//
// See docs/INTERCEPTOR.md for wiring, deadlines and failure behaviour.

